laint recording and risk evaluation are triggered.", "support_note": "The event constitutes a potential device failure requiring record maintenance under 21 CFR \u00a7 820.35.", "support_status": "supported"}], "confidence": 0.55, "evidence_links": [{"artifact_id": "mdr-annexI-sec3-risk-management-system", "artifact_type": "regulatory_extract", "relevance_note": "Requires evaluation of post-market information on hazards; the missing clinician note hinders this continuous iterative process."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.35-records", "artifact_type": "regulatory_extract", "relevance_note": "Mandates recording details of complaints including nature and corrective actions; the missing note violates this record control requirement."}, {"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-DEPLOYLOG-2007B", "artifact_type": "deployment_log", "relevance_note": "Retrieved but explicitly identified as unrelated to the incident; confirms absence of relevant technical evidence in current retrieval set."}, {"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2014A", "artifact_type": "static_analysis_output", "relevance_note": "Retrieved but explicitly identified as unrelated; highlights the gap in technical root cause analysis for this specific event."}], "missing_evidence": [], "rationale": "The incident narrative describes a 'minor' irregularity with no adverse patient outcome and is currently being handled at a monitoring level. However, the retrospective clinician note was never filed, meaning recurrence cannot be ruled out from records alone (narrative). This creates an incomplete evidence chain for risk assessment under EU MDR Annex I Section 3 requirements to evaluate post-market information on hazards (mdr-annexI-sec3-risk-management-system) and FDA QMSR record control obligations regarding complaint details (qmsr-820.35-records). Crucially, no retrieved technical artifacts (code diffs, test logs, static analysis specific to this event, or deployment logs for the affected subsystem) describe the root cause of t